Iraqi Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi postponed a plan to storm Jurf al-Sakhar, a stronghold of Iran-backed Kataib Hezbollah about 60 kilometers (37 miles) southwest of Baghdad, after a senior military commander leaked details of the operation to leaders of the ruling Coordination Framework and the Popular Mobilization Forces (PMF), Iraqi security sources told MBN. The&hellip;
The sources declined to identify the military commander, saying only that he held a senior rank and was not authorized to speak publicly.
The standoff tests whether Baghdad can move against a faction Washington designates as a terrorist organization. The government has been trying to cut off Kataib Hezbollah’s economic resources, and an Interior Ministry intelligence report, details of which MBN disclosed on Monday , documented the theft of oil from Oil Ministry pipelines in the town since 2021.
